@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-application`

-- Tests for uk-interpretation-application.l4 (ss 22, 23, 25 and Schedule 2 of the Interpretation Act 1978).
--
-- The expected values were written from the text of paras 1 to 3 and 6 of Schedule 2 (src:387-412, 428-436) and s 22(1) and 23(1),
-- as tables in a script, before the module was run; the assertions below were generated from those tables, one per provision and
-- per day, and are written out in full. A failing assertion is a finding; no expected value is edited to match the code.
-- The days chosen sit on each side of each boundary: 1850 and 1851, 1889 and 1890, the last day before the commencement
-- (31 December 1978) and the commencement day (1 January 1979).

§ `Section 22(1): the Act applies to itself`

#ASSERT `section 22(1) provides that the Interpretation Act 1978 applies to itself`

§ `Section 22(1): Acts passed on or after the commencement`

-- 1 January 1979 is the commencement day (s 26), and an Act passed on it is after the commencement of the Act as read here (fork F9).
