-- Which marks reach a given enactment.
#ASSERT NOT `a Schedule 1 paragraph with the mark applies to the enactment` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS YMD 1850 12 31, `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) (`a year is specified` 1889)
#ASSERT `a Schedule 1 paragraph with the mark applies to the enactment` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS YMD 1890 1 1, `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) (`a year is specified` 1889)
#ASSERT `a Schedule 1 paragraph with the mark applies to the enactment` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS YMD 1978 12 31, `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) (`a year is specified` 1889)
-- An Act passed after the commencement takes the whole Schedule, whatever the mark (fork F14): s 22(1).
#ASSERT `a Schedule 1 paragraph with the mark applies to the enactment` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS YMD 1979 1 1, `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) (`a date is specified` (YMD 2007 1 8))
#ASSERT `a Schedule 1 paragraph with the mark applies to the enactment` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS YMD 2000 6 1, `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) (`a date is specified` (YMD 2007 1 8))
#ASSERT NOT `a Schedule 1 paragraph with the mark applies to the enactment` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS YMD 1978 12 31, `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) (`a date is specified` (YMD 2007 1 8))
-- Subordinate legislation made after the commencement takes it as Acts do (s 23(1)); made before, no paragraph by this test (Part II names its own).
#ASSERT `a Schedule 1 paragraph with the mark applies to the enactment` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `subordinate legislation`, `the day it was passed or made` IS YMD 1979 1 1, `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) (`a year is specified` 1889)
#ASSERT `a Schedule 1 paragraph with the mark applies to the enactment` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `subordinate legislation`, `the day it was passed or made` IS YMD 2026 3 10, `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) (`a date is specified` (YMD 2007 1 8))
#ASSERT NOT `a Schedule 1 paragraph with the mark applies to the enactment` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `subordinate legislation`, `the day it was passed or made` IS YMD 1978 12 31, `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) (`a year is specified` 1889)
#ASSERT NOT `a Schedule 1 paragraph with the mark applies to the enactment` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `subordinate legislation`, `the day it was passed or made` IS YMD 1978 12 31, `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) `no year or date is specified`

